message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: 'Ontological Impoverishment: Reachable Bodies and the Freedom to Take Form'
authors:
- name: PIATRA Institute
date-released: '2026-11-01'
url: https://piatra.institute/papers/ontological-impoverishment.pdf
repository-code: https://github.com/piatra-institute/papers-ontological-impoverishment
abstract: 'This paper asks which ways of being embodied a person can reach, and defines ontological impoverishment as the institutionally avoidable foreclosure of such embodiments. The definition is formal: an embodiment is reachable when a chain of known routes leads to it through states that are physically possible, livable for the person with feasible support, and accessible on terms that leave its purposes under the person''s control. Three propositions follow: reachable sets are logically independent of income; relaxing one constraint helps only where the others already hold; and intermediate states of a transition count. Each layer has measurable indicators. The structure takes Heidegger''s being-ahead-of-itself and thrownness while setting aside his non-quantitative notion of world-poverty. It reads the experiments of Levin and colleagues on planarian regeneration, ectopic eyes, xenobots and anthrobots as enlarging physical possibility and known routes for cells and tissues, with no direct bearing on lived integration or access for persons. It separates More''s original ability from Sandberg''s negative right, and locates xenofeminism''s demands in the non-price conditions of access. A re-analysis of published Pew aggregates tests the claim that resistance to bodily enhancement belongs to the political left. In November 2021, U.S. Democrats were more often excited than Republicans about all 6 enhancement possibilities, by 8 to 11 points; religiosity divided opinion about twice as much; Democrats more often wanted stronger regulation. The evidence is American and bivariate, and the formal propositions discipline measurement without settling who decides what is worth reaching.'
